{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q27285368","formula":"C₁₄H₁₇NO₂","hill":"C14H17NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":14.0,"H":17.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"2C-G-N"},"descriptions":{"en":"2C-G-N, or 2C-G-NPH, also known as 1,4-dimethoxynaphthyl-2-ethylamine, is a psychoactive drug of the phenethylamine, 2C, and naphthylethylamine families. It is the derivative of 2C-G in which the 3,4-dimethyl groups have been extended and connected to form a second benzene ring and hence has a 2-naphthalene ring system. In his book PiHKAL (Phenethylamines I Have Known and Loved) and other publications, Alexander Shulgin lists 2C-G-N's dose as 20 to 40 mg orally and its duration as 20 to 30 hours."},"fame":3,"pubchemCid":21796713,"mass":231.29,"charge":0,"smiles":"COC1=CC(=C(C2=CC=CC=C21)OC)CCN","inchikey":"VKWQEEWEGKDTDE-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"2-(1,4-dimethoxynaphthalen-2-yl)ethanamine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"21796713","atoms":34,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.345,"y":-2.038,"z":0.142,"el":"O"},{"x":1.409,"y":2.688,"z":-0.602,"el":"O"},{"x":-4.97,"y":0.602,"z":0.655,"el":"N"},{"x":-1.322,"y":0.289,"z":-0.337,"el":"C"},{"x":0.768,"y":-0.884,"z":0.083,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.632,"y":-0.885,"z":-0.035,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.81,"y":0.293,"z":-0.464,"el":"C"},{"x":1.477,"y":0.325,"z":-0.107,"el":"C"},{"x":0.767,"y":1.498,"z":-0.41,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.624,"y":1.479,"z":-0.524,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.539,"y":0.578,"z":0.856,"el":"C"},{"x":1.478,"y":-2.057,"z":0.387,"el":"C"},{"x":2.877,"y":0.326,"z":0.011,"el":"C"},{"x":2.869,"y":-2.038,"z":0.5,"el":"C"},{"x":3.567,"y":-0.848,"z":0.313,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.575,"y":-2.836,"z":-1.015,"el":"C"},{"x":1.607,"y":3.507,"z":0.547,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.171,"y":-0.65,"z":-0.891,"el":"H"},{"x":-3.099,"y":1.052,"z":-1.205,"el":"